          {
            "commit": "461c24974158f7042bf96ca7db6cc38709e5b672",
            "subject": "llite: Remove the 2.17.58 timebomb"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-05 20:01:52.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-05 20:01:52.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-19310 lnet: do not assert a router credit implies a buffer",
        "message": "LU-19310 lnet: do not assert a router credit implies a buffer\n\nlnet_post_routed_recv_locked() takes a router buffer credit before it\nknows a buffer is available: when rbp_credits goes negative the msg is\nparked on rbp_msgs with msg_rtrcredit set and msg_kiov still NULL.\n\nDisabling routing frees the router buffer pools, and\nlnet_rtrpool_free_bufs() cancels everything left on rbp_msgs, so such a\nmsg reaches lnet_return_rx_credits_locked(), which asserts that a msg\nholding a router credit also holds a buffer:\n\n  LNetError: (lib-move.c:1047:lnet_return_rx_credits_locked())\n  ASSERTION( msg->msg_kiov != ((void *)0) ) failed\n\nSkip the buffer accounting for such a msg instead.  The credit is not\ngiven back: the pool is being torn down and its counters are reset\nregardless, and lnet_finalize() may defer the msg to another thread that\ncompletes it after that reset.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: c079e8c57a0941 (\"LU-2456 lnet: Dynamic LNet Configuration (DLC) dynamic routing\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I484cd019b9784128ce281c7d163715a3f81cbd38\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
